Third-party software in the document worker (services/worker)
-------------------------------------------------------------
The worker reads PDFs with PDFium through pypdfium2 (BSD-3-Clause or Apache-2.0). The pypdfium2 package carries the
licence texts of the libraries inside PDFium (in its dist-info/licenses folder); keep them with any copy of the
worker you distribute.

Portions of this software are copyright (c) The FreeType Project (www.freetype.org). All rights reserved.

When OCR is turned on the worker runs Tesseract (Apache-2.0) with the English and Afrikaans language data (Apache-2.0) and
Leptonica (BSD-2-Clause), which are installed in the container image and not through pip. Keep their licence texts with the image.

The worker also uses Pillow (MIT-CMU), which carries libjpeg-turbo, libpng, zlib-ng, FreeType, lcms2,
libtiff, libwebp, libavif, openjpeg, brotli, harfbuzz and xz inside its wheels; their licence texts are in
the wheel's dist-info/licenses folder. Keep them with any copy of the worker you distribute.

